The extension runs only on Audible pages (audible.com, audible.co.uk,
audible.ca, audible.com.au and audible.in) and requests no permissions. It
makes no network requests and transmits no data. The only thing stored is
the on/off state of the "Exclude AI-narrated titles" checkbox on Audible's
advanced search page, kept in that Audible site's own localStorage in your
browser. When that checkbox is on, the term -virtual_voice is added to the
search keywords you submit to Audible.
